  "caption": "Quinn's knees started crackling on every squat and staircase, and a late-night search made it sound much worse than it was.\n\nKnee noise without pain is very common and usually harmless. It's often gas bubbles in the joint fluid or tendons gliding over bone, and it doesn't mean your knee is wearing out.\n\nThings that often help: strengthening quads, glutes and calves, staying active and using stairs, and building load back gradually when returning to squats, running or hiking.\n\nIf the noise comes with pain, swelling, locking, catching, giving way, or started after an injury, it's worth getting it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
